# vendor rc creates /data/vendor_de/* subdirectories (ROM №9 avc: write on vendor_userdir_file dir)
# 🔴 07.09 (F3908): rule REMOVED - it violates an AOSP neverallow and breaks the build
# (`libsepol.report_failure` -> `Error while expanding policy`). Cannot be restored:
# neverallow is a platform restriction, not a gap on our part. If access is genuinely needed,
# solve it via relabeling (our own label instead of the platform one), not an allow on top of a denial.
# allow vendor_init vendor_userdir_file:dir { write add_name create };
# vendor rc re-creates the modem pseudo-tty symlink /dev/radio/pttyims on restart (audit A16 §4.6)
allow vendor_init mtk_radio_device:lnk_file unlink;
